            <ArticleTitle>[Hybrid revascularisation in a patient with multivessel and left main coronary disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>270-3; discussion 274</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>According to current guidelines surgical revascularisation is a gold standard of treatment in patients with multivessel and left main coronary disease. Hybrid revascularisation, in two stages: first - minimally invasive direct coronary artery bypass grafting procedure with left internal mammary artery conduit to left anterior descending artery and second stage - percutaneus coronary intervention with drug eluting stent in non-left anterior descending vessels may be safe and effective alternative in patients with multivessel and left main coronary disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
